## GML Examples
# Minimal Design -- GML Examples

Reference cards showing how minimal spatial intent translates to GML.

## Title Card (brand logo + hero image, near-empty)

```html
<section image-layout="behind" background-color="#8ea3a8" card-margin-hidden="true">
  <img class="accent-image" type="image" src="..." alt="three surfboards on the beach">
  <div class="body">
    <labels><label color="#B0BCBC" variant="solid">surf and coastal lifestyle brand overview</label></labels>
    <img src="..." source="image.custom">
    <p></p>
  </div>
</section>
```
*Title card has a brand logo image, a label, and nothing else. The beach photograph does all the work.*

## Breather / Quote Card (DISPLAY + dramatic image)

```html
<section image-layout="behind" background-color="#1B2C1A">
  <img class="accent-image" type="image" src="..." alt="rolling green hills">
  <div class="body">
    <display style="text-align: center" size="lg">
      <span text-color="#F1EBDF"><em>"Where</em><b><em> Stories </em></b><em>Find You."</em></span>
    </display>
  </div>
</section>
```
*4 words in DISPLAY over a moody landscape. Creates pacing.*

## DISPLAY + Label Card (editorial section divider)

```html
<section image-layout="behind" background-color="#2C1810" vertical-align="end">
  <img class="accent-image" type="image" src="..." alt="hands selecting coffee beans on wooden table">
  <div class="body">
    <labels><label color="#D4A574" variant="solid">Chapter Two</label></labels>
    <display size="lg">The <span text-color="#D4A574">Craft</span></display>
    <p><span text-color="#FFFFFF">Where patience becomes flavor.</span></p>
  </div>
</section>
```
*Label + DISPLAY combination. Label provides editorial structure, DISPLAY provides emotional weight. Background-color shows through the image overlay.*

## Content Card (behind image + solidBoxes with colored items)

```html
<section image-layout="behind" background-color="#251B1C">
  <img class="accent-image" type="image" src="..." alt="espresso crema close-up">
  <div class="body">
    <labels><label color="#FFEA58" variant="solid">Chapter 2</label></labels>
    <h1>The Rise of <b>Crema</b></h1>
    <h4><span text-color="#FBF8F0">Mid-20th Century — Pressure, craft, and the golden layer</span></h4>
    <smart-layout color="#663e20" cellsize="10" variant="solidBoxes">
      <smart-layout-item color="#E9D5A8">
        <h4><b>The Challenge</b></h4>
        <p>Steam-only machines scorched grounds. Consistency remained elusive.</p>
      </smart-layout-item>
      <smart-layout-item color="#BD925C">
        <h4><span text-color="#FBF8F0"><b>Gaggia's Revolution</b></span></h4>
        <p><span text-color="#FBF8F0">Achille Gaggia's 1947 piston-driven patent hit 8-10 bars of pressure — and crema appeared.</span></p>
      </smart-layout-item>
      <smart-layout-item color="#A56D3D">
        <h4><span text-color="#FBF8F0"><b>Faema E61 (1961)</b></span></h4>
        <p><span text-color="#FBF8F0">Electric pump, continuous water flow, advanced brew groups. The modern machine was born.</span></p>
      </smart-layout-item>
    </smart-layout>
  </div>
</section>
```
*Three solidBoxes on behind image. Each item has a distinct tonal color. Label provides structural context. text-color spans for readability on dark bg.*

## Editorial Card (DISPLAY + food photography)

```html
<section image-layout="behind" vertical-align="start">
  <img class="accent-image" type="image" src="..." alt="strawberry basil cocktail">
  <div class="body">
    <display size="md">Strawberry &amp; <span text-color="#C34626"><b>Basil</b></span></display>
    <labels><label variant="plain">Aromatic Harmony</label></labels>
    <p>Shared volatile esters and aldehydes create a sweet,
    herbaceous synergy that feels both surprising and inevitable.</p>
  </div>
</section>
```
*DISPLAY as primary element, label as metadata, one paragraph. Food image does the heavy lifting.*

## Columns + Smart Layout (asymmetric split with colored panel)

```html
<section image-layout="blank" background-color="#3b4428">
  <div class="body">
    <h1><span text-color="#FFFFFF">The Taste of Authenticity</span></h1>
    <columns colwidths="[65,35]">
      <div data-vertical-align="center">
        <img src="..." alt="olive oil and bread">
      </div>
      <div data-vertical-align="center">
        <smart-layout color="#d4ad4d" cellsize="10" variant="sideLineText">
