## GML Examples
# Minimal Design -- GML Examples

Reference cards showing how minimal spatial intent translates to GML.

## Title Card (brand logo + hero image, near-empty)

```html
<section image-layout="behind" background-color="#8ea3a8" card-margin-hidden="true">
  <img class="accent-image" type="image" src="..." alt="three surfboards on the beach">
  <div class="body">
    <labels><label color="#B0BCBC" variant="solid">surf and coastal lifestyle brand overview</label></labels>
    <img src="..." source="image.custom">
    <p></p>
  </div>
</section>
```
*Title card has a brand logo image, a label, and nothing else. The beach photograph does all the work.*

## Breather / Quote Card (DISPLAY + dramatic image)

```html
<section image-layout="behind" background-color="#1B2C1A">
  <img class="accent-image" type="image" src="..." alt="rolling green hills">
  <div class="body">
    <display style="text-align: center" size="lg">
      <span text-color="#F1EBDF"><em>"Where</em><b><em> Stories </em></b><em>Find You."</em></span>
    </display>
  </div>
</section>
```
*4 words in DISPLAY over a moody landscape. Creates pacing.*

## DISPLAY + Label Card (editorial section divider)

```html
<section image-layout="behind" background-color="#2C1810" vertical-align="end">
  <img class="accent-image" type="image" src="..." alt="hands selecting coffee beans on wooden table">
  <div class="body">
    <labels><label color="#D4A574" variant="solid">Chapter Two</label></labels>
    <display size="lg">The <span text-color="#D4A574">Craft</span></display>
    <p><span text-color="#FFFFFF">Where patience becomes flavor.</span></p>
  </div>
</section>
```
*Label + DISPLAY combination. Label provides editorial structure, DISPLAY provides emotional weight. Background-color shows through the image overlay.*

## Content Card (behind image + solidBoxes with colored items)

```html
<section image-layout="behind" background-color="#251B1C">
  <img class="accent-image" type="image" src="..." alt="espresso crema close-up">
  <div class="body">
    <labels><label color="#FFEA58" variant="solid">Chapter 2</label></labels>
    <h1>The Rise of <b>Crema</b></h1>
    <h4><span text-color="#FBF8F0">Mid-20th Century — Pressure, craft, and the golden layer</span></h4>
    <smart-layout color="#663e20" cellsize="10" variant="solidBoxes">
      <smart-layout-item color="#E9D5A8">
        <h4><b>The Challenge</b></h4>
        <p>Steam-only machines scorched grounds. Consistency remained elusive.</p>
      </smart-layout-item>
      <smart-layout-item color="#BD925C">
        <h4><span text-color="#FBF8F0"><b>Gaggia's Revolution</b></span></h4>
        <p><span text-color="#FBF8F0">Achille Gaggia's 1947 piston-driven patent hit 8-10 bars of pressure — and crema appeared.</span></p>
      </smart-layout-item>
      <smart-layout-item color="#A56D3D">
        <h4><span text-color="#FBF8F0"><b>Faema E61 (1961)</b></span></h4>
        <p><span text-color="#FBF8F0">Electric pump, continuous water flow, advanced brew groups. The modern machine was born.</span></p>
      </smart-layout-item>
    </smart-layout>
  </div>
</section>
```
*Three solidBoxes on behind image. Each item has a distinct tonal color. Label provides structural context. text-color spans for readability on dark bg.*

## Editorial Card (DISPLAY + food photography)

```html
<section image-layout="behind" vertical-align="start">
  <img class="accent-image" type="image" src="..." alt="strawberry basil cocktail">
  <div class="body">
    <display size="md">Strawberry &amp; <span text-color="#C34626"><b>Basil</b></span></display>
    <labels><label variant="plain">Aromatic Harmony</label></labels>
    <p>Shared volatile esters and aldehydes create a sweet,
    herbaceous synergy that feels both surprising and inevitable.</p>
  </div>
</section>
```
*DISPLAY as primary element, label as metadata, one paragraph. Food image does the heavy lifting.*

## Columns + Smart Layout (asymmetric split with colored panel)

```html
<section image-layout="blank" background-color="#3b4428">
  <div class="body">
    <h1><span text-color="#FFFFFF">The Taste of Authenticity</span></h1>
    <columns colwidths="[65,35]">
      <div data-vertical-align="center">
        <img src="..." alt="olive oil and bread">
      </div>
      <div data-vertical-align="center">
        <smart-layout color="#d4ad4d" cellsize="10" variant="sideLineText">
          <smart-layout-item color="#d4ad4d">
            <h4><span text-color="#FFFFFF">Fruity Aroma</span></h4>
            <p><span text-color="#FFFFFF">Distinctive banana notes</span></p>
          </smart-layout-item>
          <smart-layout-item color="#d4ad4d">
            <h4><span text-color="#FFFFFF">Complex Profile</span></h4>
            <p><span text-color="#FFFFFF">Subtle bitterness and sharpness</span></p>
          </smart-layout-item>
          <smart-layout-item color="#d4ad4d">
            <h4><span text-color="#FFFFFF">Terroir Expression</span></h4>
            <p><span text-color="#FFFFFF">Each drop tells the story of land, family, and generations</span></p>
          </smart-layout-item>
        </smart-layout>
      </div>
    </columns>
  </div>
</section>
```
*Asymmetric columns: large image left, sideLineText right. Dark bg-color with white text. Gold accent on smart layout lines.*

## Behind-Image + DISPLAY Title Card (cinematic opener)

```html
<section image-layout="behind" background-color="#1A1A2E" vertical-align="end" card-margin-hidden="true">
  <img class="accent-image" type="image" src="..." alt="aerial view of luxury resort infinity pool at golden hour, warm light reflecting on water">
  <div class="body">
    <labels><label color="#C9A96E" variant="solid">The Experience</label></labels>
    <display size="lg"><span text-color="#C9A96E">Sanctuary</span></display>
    <p><span text-color="#FFFFFF">Where the horizon meets intention.</span></p>
  </div>
</section>
```
*Title card: behind-image with DISPLAY. Text anchored at bottom. Label above. Accent color on the emotional word. Near-empty — the photograph does all the work.*

## Behind-Image Content Card (editorial feature)

```html
<section image-layout="behind" background-color="#2D2B28" vertical-align="start">
  <img class="accent-image" type="image" src="..." alt="architect examining building model in studio, natural window light, concrete walls">
  <div class="body">
    <labels><label color="#B8A088" variant="solid">Chapter Two</label></labels>
    <h1>The <span text-color="#B8A088">Process</span></h1>
    <h4><span text-color="#FFFFFF">Every line is a conversation between light and material.</span></h4>
  </div>
</section>
```
*Behind-image content card. Sparse — heading + one sentence. Label provides editorial navigation. text-color for readability on dark image.*

## Bg-Color Card with solidBoxes (editorial grid on color)

```html
<section image-layout="blank" background-color="#E8E0D4">
  <div class="body">
    <labels><label color="#5C4A3A" variant="solid">The Collection</label></labels>
    <h1>Three <span text-color="#5C4A3A">Pillars</span></h1>
    <smart-layout color="#5C4A3A" cellsize="10" variant="solidBoxes">
      <smart-layout-item color="#D4C4B0">
        <h4><b>Origin</b></h4>
        <p>Single-estate, hand-selected.</p>
      </smart-layout-item>
      <smart-layout-item color="#C8B49A">
        <h4><b>Craft</b></h4>
        <p>Slow-roasted at source.</p>
      </smart-layout-item>
      <smart-layout-item color="#B8A488">
        <h4><span text-color="#FFFFFF"><b>Ritual</b></span></h4>
        <p><span text-color="#FFFFFF">Brewed with patience.</span></p>
      </smart-layout-item>
    </smart-layout>
  </div>
</section>
```
*solidBoxes on a warm bg-color card (no image). Each item has tonal color variation. Max 3 items, one sentence each. This is the "editorial grid" pattern — structured content on a colored surface.*

## Behind-Image + Bg-Color Alternation (3-card rhythm)

Card A (behind-image):
```html
<section image-layout="behind" background-color="#1B3A2D" vertical-align="end">
  <img class="accent-image" type="image" src="..." alt="morning mist over tea plantation, rolling hills">
  <div class="body">
    <labels><label color="#A8C4A0" variant="solid">Origin</label></labels>
    <display size="lg">From the <span text-color="#A8C4A0">Hills</span></display>
  </div>
</section>
```

Card B (bg-color only):
```html
<section image-layout="blank" background-color="#F0EBE3">
  <div class="body">
    <labels><label color="#1B3A2D" variant="solid">The Process</label></labels>
    <h1>Hand-Picked at <span text-color="#1B3A2D">Dawn</span></h1>
    <h4>Each leaf selected in the first light. No machines. No shortcuts.</h4>
  </div>
</section>
```

Card C (behind-image):
```html
<section image-layout="behind" background-color="#2C1F14" vertical-align="start">
  <img class="accent-image" type="image" src="..." alt="close-up of hands rolling tea leaves on wooden surface">
  <div class="body">
    <labels><label color="#D4A574" variant="solid">Chapter Three</label></labels>
    <h1>The <span text-color="#D4A574">Craft</span></h1>
    <h4><span text-color="#FFFFFF">Generations of knowledge in every gesture.</span></h4>
  </div>
</section>
```
*Three-card rhythm: behind-image (atmospheric) -> bg-color (structured) -> behind-image (editorial). This alternation is the signature minimal pattern.*

## Asymmetric Columns: Narrow Text + Wide Image

```html
<section image-layout="blank" background-color="#1E1E2A">
  <div class="body">
    <columns colwidths="[35,65]">
      <div data-vertical-align="center">
        <labels><label color="#8B7EC8" variant="solid">Portfolio</label></labels>
        <h1><span text-color="#8B7EC8">Forma</span> Tower</h1>
        <p><span text-color="#FFFFFF">Glass and steel in dialogue. 47 stories of light.</span></p>
      </div>
      <div data-vertical-align="center">
        <img src="..." alt="modern glass tower reflecting sunset, angular geometry">
      </div>
    </columns>
  </div>
</section>
```
*Asymmetric columns: 35% text, 65% image. Both columns have content — never leave a column empty. Dark bg-color, white text for readability.*

